# In-band size reports on, so that what a resize tells the child — the grid
# and how big one cell is — lands in the golden beside the screen it reflowed.
# Nothing a recording holds asks the terminal for its size in pixels.
out "\x1b[?2048h"
# A line exactly as wide as the grid, and then a grid half as wide. What was
# one row has to become two, the first of them marked as running on — a screen
# that lost the tail instead is what this holds against.
out "abcdefghijklmnopqrst"
resize 10 4 8 16
